From 352e4b76e2f54f13553ca22ff1e9d14e84e2875c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerd Hoffmann <kraxel@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:34:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ShellPkg: disable mmx and sse instructions

RH-Author: Gerd Hoffmann <kraxel@redhat.com>
RH-MergeRequest: 145: ShellPkg: disable mmx and sse instructions
RH-Jira: RHEL-257729
RH-Acked-by: Luigi Leonardi <None>
RH-Commit: [1/1] 602d6043de69d9e8087a1229f5dd0a8ec0e9f085

Add gcc command line options to disable the usage
of MMX and SSE instructions.

Without that gcc may generate instructions like
'vmovaps %xmm9,-0x80(%rbp)', which in turn will
trigger 'Invalid Opcode' exceptions.

Signed-off-by: Gerd Hoffmann <kraxel@redhat.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/pull/13123
---
 ShellPkg/ShellPkg.dsc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ShellPkg/ShellPkg.dsc b/ShellPkg/ShellPkg.dsc
index 94d95de0eb..453c081a68 100644
--- a/ShellPkg/ShellPkg.dsc
+++ b/ShellPkg/ShellPkg.dsc
@@ -158,3 +158,4 @@
 
 [BuildOptions]
   *_*_*_CC_FLAGS = -D DISABLE_NEW_DEPRECATED_INTERFACES
+  GCC:*_*_X64_CC_FLAGS = -mno-mmx -mno-sse
-- 
2.55.0

